WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:08.652
This short guide shows ISSV teachers how to run a virtual Sunday class with Google Classroom and Google Meet.

00:00:09.252 --> 00:00:15.141
First, make sure you’re signed in with your ISSV school account, not a personal Gmail.

00:00:15.291 --> 00:00:21.757
The admin has already created your class and added your students, so it’s waiting on your Classroom home page.

00:00:22.357 --> 00:00:28.481
You only need to do this next part once. In your class, click the gear icon to open Settings.

00:00:28.631 --> 00:00:31.960
Under General, find Meet link, and generate a link.

00:00:32.381 --> 00:00:35.411
Turn on Visible to students, then click Save.

00:00:36.531 --> 00:00:42.591
Now your class has one Meet link for every virtual Sunday. Please don’t post links anywhere else.

00:00:43.191 --> 00:00:46.307
On Saturday, post a quick reminder in the Stream.

00:00:46.457 --> 00:00:53.946
Something like: Virtual class tomorrow at ten. Join from the Meet link on this page, signed in with your school account.

00:00:55.357 --> 00:01:00.222
On Sunday, open the Meet at about 9:50, straight from your class page.

00:01:00.372 --> 00:01:07.627
Click the Host controls shield, and turn on Host management. Now you can mute everyone and decide who joins.

00:01:07.777 --> 00:01:12.429
Students signed in with a personal account will show up as asking to join.

00:01:12.579 --> 00:01:18.105
Only admit names you recognize, and remind them to use their school account next time.

00:01:18.255 --> 00:01:23.057
When class is over, click the red button, and choose End the call for everyone.

00:01:23.755 --> 00:01:28.450
Then post any homework in Classwork, and take attendance from the People list.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:38.295
That’s it! The written steps are on the Online Classes page of the school website. If a class or setting is missing, email the school office.
